      "title": "SOME/IP: Respect endianness parameter for strings",
      "message": "SOME/IP: Respect endianness parameter for strings\n\nActually do something with the endianness parameter for a string.\nBased on the issue filed, assume that a string that is configured\nas UTF-16LE also has a little endian length parameter if that length\nparameter is more than one octet. (The spec is a little vague on this,\nperhaps they could even be different endianness and there needs be\nmultiple configuration parameters?) Fixes #17058\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2020-12-04T22:41:44.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
